FYI, to reproduce the error we needed to:
* Comment out the following lines from ESIntegTestCase.java:
```
//        if (randomBoolean()) {
//            builder.put(IndexSettings.BLOOM_FILTER_ID_FIELD_ENABLED_SETTING.getKey(), randomBoolean());
//        }
```
* Change the following line in FlushIT.java:
```
.put(IndexingMemoryController.SHARD_MEMORY_INTERVAL_TIME_SETTING.getKey(), randomTimeValue(10, 10, "ms"))
```
Then most of times executing 
```
./gradlew ':server:internalClusterTest' --tests "org.elasticsearch.indices.flush.FlushIT.testFlushOnInactive" -Dtests.random=$RANDOM  -Dtests.seed=38FC56033AE2DC88 -Dtests.locale=en-IN -Dtests.timezone=Europe/Zaporozhye -Druntime.java=17
```
makes the problem appear.
